<title>USA: USDA boosts GSM-102 to Mexico by $150 Mln.</title>
<headline>USDA boosts GSM-102 to Mexico by $150 Mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said  Friday it released an additional $150 million in short-term GSM-102  export credit guarantees to Mexico.</p>
<p>With the addition, $1.225 billion of the export credits has been offered  to facilitate sales of U.S. ag products to Mexico in fiscal 1997,  which ends September 30.</p>
<p>Terms of the credits and the list of commodities eligible for coverage  remained the same.</p>
</text>
